          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A patient's CBC confirms anaemia (Hb 7.5 g/dL) with an MCV of 68 fL. You have gr</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A patient's CBC confirms anaemia (Hb 7.5 g/dL) with an MCV of 68 fL. You have graded the severity and classified the anaemia by MCV. According to the systematic five-step workup, what is your next step?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Order serum ferritin and haemoglobin electrophoresis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>These are targeted second-line tests (step 5). You must first calculate the RPI and review the peripheral smear before ordering them.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Start empirical iron supplementation</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Treatment before completing the diagnostic workup risks masking the underlying cause. The framework requires finishing investigation before starting therapy.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Calculate the reticulocyte production index</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Step 3 is calculating the RPI to determine whether the marrow is compensating (RPI &gt; 2, suggesting destruction or loss) or underproducing (RPI &lt; 2, pointing to a production defect).</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Refer for a bone marrow biopsy</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Bone marrow biopsy is reserved for unexplained cytopenias. The systematic workup requires RPI, peripheral smear review, and targeted blood tests first.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Follow the sequence: (1) confirm/grade, (2) check MCV, (3) calculate RPI, (4) review peripheral smear, (5) run targeted tests. After MCV, the RPI is the next step."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! The five steps in order are: confirm and grade → MCV → RPI → peripheral smear → targeted second-line tests. Each step informs the next."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
